{
  "name": "Job Agent 01 — Ingest & Score",
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "saveManualExecutions": true,
    "callerPolicy": "workflowsFromSameOwner"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -460,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 340,
        "content": "## 01 — Ingest & Score\n\nRuns daily at 09:00. The webhook is a bonus early trigger; Distill only allows 30 calls a month, so the schedule is the real clock.\n\n**Write-first rule:** the raw payload hits `raw_inbox` before anything parses it. A webhook fire is not replayable and you only get 30.\n\n**Everything is configured from `.env`** — settings and keys are read at runtime, your profile is baked in by `npm run setup`. There is nothing to fill in inside this workflow.\n\nYou still need to connect **Google Sheets** and **Gmail** under Credentials.\n\n⚠️ Don't edit code in this editor — it is generated. Edit `n8n/code/*.js`, run `npm run setup`, re-import."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "trigger-schedule",
      "name": "Daily Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 9 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "trigger-webhook",
      "name": "Distill Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        140
      ],
      "webhookId": "distill-jobs",
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "distill-jobs",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "load-profile",
      "name": "Load Profile",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:00-load-profile.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "gmail-fetch",
      "name": "Fetch Distill Emails",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        480,
        -60
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "message",
        "operation": "getAll",
        "returnAll": true,
        "simple": false,
        "filters": {
          "q": "label:distill/jobs is:unread newer_than:2d"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "Distill's email action is the unmetered data pipe. Gmail filter: subject contains [DISTILL] -> label distill/jobs, skip inbox."
    },
    {
      "id": "norm-email",
      "name": "Normalize Email Payload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        720,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:02-normalize-email.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "norm-webhook",
      "name": "Normalize Webhook Payload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        720,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:01-normalize-webhook.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sheet-raw",
      "name": "Append Raw Inbox",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        980,
        40
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "append",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.sheet_id }}"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "raw_inbox"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData",
          "value": {},
          "matchingColumns": []
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "Write-first. Nothing downstream can lose the day's payload."
    },
    {
      "id": "parse-diff",
      "name": "Parse Distill Diff",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1220,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:03-parse-diff.js"
      },
      "notes": "Tune NOISE here first. Applicant counts and '2 hours ago' will otherwise regenerate the same jobs every day."
    },
    {
      "id": "req-extract",
      "name": "Build Extract Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1460,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:req-extract.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "claude-extract",
      "name": "AI: Extract Jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1700,
        40
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $json._llm.url }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.body) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 180000
        },
        "specifyHeaders": "json",
        "jsonHeaders": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.headers) }}"
      },
      "notes": "Endpoint, auth header and body all come from $json._llm, which lib.js builds for whichever LLM_PROVIDER is set in .env. Nothing here is provider-specific, so switching AI never touches this node."
    },
    {
      "id": "norm-extracted",
      "name": "Normalize Extracted",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1940,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:04-normalize-extracted.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sheet-read-jobs",
      "name": "Read Existing Jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        2180,
        40
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "read",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.sheet_id }}"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "jobs"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "One read for the whole run. A per-item lookup would blow the Sheets quota on a busy day."
    },
    {
      "id": "dedupe",
      "name": "Dedupe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2420,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:05-dedupe.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hard-filters",
      "name": "Hard Filters",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2660,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:06-hard-filters.js"
      },
      "notes": "Free and instant. Typically removes 50-60% before a single token is spent."
    },
    {
      "id": "if-passed",
      "name": "IF Passed Hard Filters",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2900,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "passed",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.filtered_out }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "false",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "req-score",
      "name": "Build Score Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3140,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:req-score.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "claude-score",
      "name": "AI: Score Job",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        3380,
        -80
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $json._llm.url }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.body) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 180000,
          "batching": {
            "batch": {
              "batchSize": 4,
              "batchInterval": 1500
            }
          }
        },
        "specifyHeaders": "json",
        "jsonHeaders": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.headers) }}"
      },
      "notes": "Endpoint, auth header and body all come from $json._llm, which lib.js builds for whichever LLM_PROVIDER is set in .env. Nothing here is provider-specific, so switching AI never touches this node."
    },
    {
      "id": "merge-score",
      "name": "Merge Score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3620,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:07-merge-score.js"
      },
      "notes": "Applies the thresholds from Load Profile and sets the final status: queued / review / skipped."
    },
    {
      "id": "strip-internal",
      "name": "Strip Internal Fields",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3860,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "// Drop the working fields so the sheet only gets real columns.\nreturn $input.all().map((item) => {\n  const { _body, filtered_out, filter_reason, ...rest } = item.json;\n  return { json: rest };\n});"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sheet-write-jobs",
      "name": "Write Jobs Sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        4100,
        40
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "append",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.sheet_id }}"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "jobs"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData",
          "value": {},
          "matchingColumns": []
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "if-review",
      "name": "IF Needs Review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        4340,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "isreview",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.status }}",
              "rightValue": "review",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "notifyon",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.notify }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "telegram-review",
      "name": "Telegram Review Card",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        4580,
        -60
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.telegram_chat_id }}",
        "text": "=*{{ $json.score }}/100 — {{ $json.title }}*\n{{ $json.company }} · {{ $json.location }} ({{ $json.remote_type }})\n\n{{ $json.score_reason }}\n\nGaps: {{ $json.missing_skills || 'none noted' }}\n\n{{ $json.canonical_url }}\n\nSet status to `queued` in the sheet to apply.",
        "additionalFields": {
          "parse_mode": "Markdown",
          "disable_web_page_preview": true
        }
      },
      "notes": "Borderline jobs come to you instead of being auto-applied or silently dropped."
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-quota",
      "name": "Quota note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -460,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### Distill quota\n\n30 webhook calls / month ÷ 1 per day = exactly 30 days. A 31-day month runs out on the last day.\n\nThat is why the Schedule Trigger is the clock and the email action is the pipe. The webhook here is a bonus early trigger, not the data path.\n\nIf `raw_inbox` gets no rows two runs running, a monitor selector broke or a login expired. Check before assuming nobody is hiring."
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Daily Trigger": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Load Profile",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Distill Webhook": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Load Profile",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Load Profile": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Fetch Distill Emails",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          },
          {
            "node": "Normalize Webhook Payload",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Fetch Distill Emails": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Normalize Email Payload",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Normalize Email Payload": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Append Raw Inbox",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Normalize Webhook Payload": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Append Raw Inbox",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Append Raw Inbox": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Parse Distill Diff",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Parse Distill Diff": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Build Extract Request",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Build Extract Request": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "AI: Extract Jobs",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "AI: Extract Jobs": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Normalize Extracted",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Normalize Extracted": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Read Existing Jobs",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Read Existing Jobs": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Dedupe",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Dedupe": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Hard Filters",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Hard Filters": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "IF Passed Hard Filters",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "IF Passed Hard Filters": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Build Score Request",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "Strip Internal Fields",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Build Score Request": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "AI: Score Job",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "AI: Score Job": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Merge Score",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Merge Score": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Strip Internal Fields",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Strip Internal Fields": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Write Jobs Sheet",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Write Jobs Sheet": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "IF Needs Review",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "IF Needs Review": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Telegram Review Card",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        []
      ]
    }
  },
  "pinData": {}
}
